{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QTraceCyclic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.qTrace_peel_physical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.qTrace_peel_physical","kind":"theorem","line":338,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovPeel.lean#L338-L345","doc":"**The peel at the physical weight**, with its forced scalar: `z = q³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.qTrace_peel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.qTrace_peel","kind":"theorem","line":328,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovPeel.lean#L328-L336","doc":"**The peel, at algebra level.** `tr_w(ι(x) · σ_last) = z · tr_w(x)` — Markov move II,\nconditional on the weight admitting a peel scalar at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.trace_peel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.trace_peel","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovPeel.lean#L283-L326","doc":"**The peel, at matrix level.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.trace_siteWeight_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.trace_siteWeight_mul","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovPeel.lean#L275-L281","doc":"Rewriting a weighted trace as a sum over basis states. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.extendSite_mul_lastBraid_diag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.extendSite_mul_lastBraid_diag","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovPeel.lean#L228-L273","doc":"**The diagonal of `(X ⊗ 1) · Ř` collapses to one term.**\n\nThe two supports intersect tightly: `X ⊗ 1` forces the new site to be preserved, and `Ř`\nforces every site but the two it acts on to be preserved, leaving only site `m` free — and\n`Ř`'s swap entry cannot fire there because it would need that free value to equal both of the\nothers. So only the diagonal survives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.peel_scalar_of_physical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.peel_scalar_of_physical","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovPeel.lean#L212-L220","doc":"The converse: at `w = (1, q²)` the partial trace really is the scalar `q³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.peel_weight_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.peel_weight_eq","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovPeel.lean#L202-L210","doc":"With the scale fixed by `w 0 = 1`, the forced weight is `(1, q²)` and the forced peel\nscalar is `q³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.peel_forces_physical_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.peel_forces_physical_weight","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovPeel.lean#L186-L200","doc":"**The peel scalar exists exactly at the physical weight.**\n\nIf the weighted partial trace of `Ř` over the new site is the *same* scalar `z` whichever\nvalue the surviving site carries — which is precisely what a peel `tr(xσ) = z·tr(x)` needs —\nthen `w 0 · q = w 1 · qi`, i.e. `w 1 = q² · w 0`, and `z = w 1 · q`.\n\nSo the corpus's weight `K = diag(1, q²)` is forced by the peel, not chosen for it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.rCheck_diag_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.rCheck_diag_apply","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovPeel.lean#L169-L172","doc":"The diagonal entries of `Ř`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.heckeActionN_tower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.heckeActionN_tower","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovPeel.lean#L155-L165","doc":"**The tower square commutes**: acting after adding a strand is extending the action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.extendSite_strandBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.extendSite_strandBraid","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovPeel.lean#L118-L153","doc":"The site extension of a strand braiding is the corresponding strand braiding one level\nup. This is the one place the `Fin` arithmetic of the tower is done. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.tower_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.tower_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovPeel.lean#L113-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.tower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.tower","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovPeel.lean#L101-L111","doc":"**The tower map** `H_{m+1}(q) → H_{m+2}(q)`, adding a strand on the right. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.coxA_castSucc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.coxA_castSucc","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovPeel.lean#L94-L99","doc":"The type-`A` Coxeter matrix restricts along `castSucc`: strands `0 … m−1` of `H_{m+2}(q)`\ncarry the same Coxeter data they had in `H_{m+1}(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.extendSiteHom_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.extendSiteHom_apply","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovPeel.lean#L82-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.extendSiteHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.extendSiteHom","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovPeel.lean#L74-L80","doc":"**The site extension** `X ↦ X ⊗ 1`: act by `X` on the first `m+1` sites, do nothing to\nthe new one. An algebra map, because `idTensorHom` and reindexing both are. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.lastSplit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel.lastSplit","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovPeel.lean#L70-L72","doc":"Splitting a state of `V^{⊗(m+2)}` into its last site and the first `m+1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}